    <title>
      <narrative xml:lang="en">NESA Center Silk Road Future Leaders Seminar 01-21: "Strategic Leadership for Regional Security"</narrative>
    </title>
    <description type="1">
      <narrative xml:lang="en">The Near East and South Asia Center for Strategic Studies (NESA) will host a modified version of its popular Silk Road Future Leaders Seminar with a one-day webinar on Strategic Leadership for Regional Security. The webinarwhich features several internationally-recognized scholar-practitioners from the NESA Center facultyis intended to re-engage alumni from previous iterations of the Silk Road Future Leaders Seminar that were conducted in person in Washington, DC. Discussions will be held under the Chatham House Rule (off-the-record) and will not be recorded to promote an open exchange and debate of ideas and assessments. The webinar will be conducted in English on Zoom with simultaneous interpretation in Russian.</narrative>
    </description>
